{% extends "base.html.j2" %}

{% from "_formhelpers.html.j2" import render_field %}
{% from "_projecthelpers.html.j2" import navbar, cancel, render_datasets %}

{% block content %}

{% include '_header.html.j2' %}

<div class="mui-panel">
  {{ navbar(project, "Ingest") }}

  <h1>Manage ingest share for session "{{ ds.name }}" in project "{{ project.name }}"</h1>
  
  {% include '_flash.html.j2' %}
  <p>An ingest network share is a temporary Windows network share (SMB/CIFS) with temporary credentials
  that can be created on-demand for a session.
  Mapping it on machines that are operated with system accounts,
  such as microscope computers, allows importing data into a session using the identity of the operator
  and not the system account. At the same time, it avoids issues with saving credentials
  on machines that are used by many users.</p>
  <p>That way, data can be saved directly in the correct location with correct ownership
  and access permissions using all data acquisition tools and most operating systems.
  The ingest GUI FIXME link etc? helps managing the shares and sessions on the client machine.
  </p>
  <p>
  Windows only allows one set of credentials per session and remote host. The management interface creates all ingest shares for the same user
  with the same credentials so that they can be open in parallel. Ingest shares for different users
  cannot coexist, however. Any active shares by other users have to be closed for that reason. Active shares
  can be listed with <code>net use</code> on the command line and closed with <code>net use &lt;drive letter or path&gt; /delete</code>.
  Please note that shares opened with <code>\\&lt;host&gt;\&lt;share&gt;</code> in the Explorer remain active even after the Explorer window
  is closed. They can only be unmapped via the command line or the Microsoft Management Console.
  </p>
  {% if ds.shareinfo %}
    {% with si = ds.shareinfo %}  
      <h2>Access using Windows Explorer</h2>
      <div>
        <label for="urlwin">Address</label>
        <input id="urlwin" value="\\{{ si.smb_host }}\{{ si.share_name}}" readonly style="width: 100%"/>

        <label for="username">Username</label>
        <input id="username" value="{{ si.workgroup }}\{{ si.username }}" readonly style="width: 100%"/>

        <label for="passwordwin">Password</label>
        <input id="passwordwin" value="{{ si.password }}" readonly style="width: 100%"/>
      </div>
      <h2>Map as network drive Z: on Windows</h2>
      <input id="netusewin" value="net use /persistent:no z: \\{{ si.smb_host }}\{{ si.share_name}} {{ si.password }} /USER:{{ si.workgroup }}\{{ si.username }}" readonly style="width: 100%"/>
      <h2>Unmap network drive Z: on Windows</h2>
      <input id="netusedeletewin" value="net use z: /delete" readonly style="width: 100%"/>
      <h2>Unmap after opening in Windows Explorer</h2>
      <input id="netusedeletewin2" value="net use \\{{ si.smb_host }}\{{ si.share_name}} /delete" readonly style="width: 100%"/>
      <h2>Access on Linux or OS X using a file manager</h2>
      <div>
        <label for="url">Address</label>
        <input id="url" value="smb://{{ si.username }}@{{ si.smb_host }}/{{ si.share_name }}" readonly style="width: 100%"/>
        
        <label for="password">Password</label>
        <input id="password" value="{{ si.password }}" readonly style="width: 100%"/>
      </div>
    {% endwith %}
  {%endif%}
  <form
      method=post
      action="{{ url_for("share_dataset", name=project.name, dataset=ds.name) }}"
      class="mui-form"
  >
    {{ form.csrf_token }}
    {{ form.op }}
    <p>
      <input
        type="submit"
        class="mui-btn mui-btn--raised mui-btn--primary"
        value="{% if ds.shareinfo %}Close{% else %}Create{% endif %} ingest share of session '{{ ds.name }}'"
      />
      {{ cancel(project) }}
    </p>
  </form>
</div>
{% endblock content %}